[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558870111","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2558870111","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2558870111,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YhUJf","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T04:09:58Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T04:09:58Z","body":"It's been slow around the end of the year. I would like a hero to help try the code and post videos. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558870111/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2559012062","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2559012062","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2559012062,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yh2ze","user":{"login":"31","id":331300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/331300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/31","html_url":"https://github.com/31","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T06:41:17Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T06:41:17Z","body":"Will do! I don't have much of a stress test, but some relatively dynamic stuff going on. 😄\r\n\r\n> (https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9933#issuecomment-2475291288)\r\n> Hello! I recently made a plugin called [VertexHandles](https://github.com/celyk/godot-useful-stuff/tree/main/addons/VertexHandles) that allows you to edit the vertices of a Mesh when placed under a MeshInstance3D. The code could be modified to generate a mesh based on the points instead. I hope this helps!\r\n\r\nI tweaked it a bit to work with the current PR: https://gist.github.com/31/ac9ebdfc9b702ec135b3446d63d7a86e. I'm not actually all that used to classic multi-view ortho editing, but it works nicely here because it simply uses the camera projection plane. I think incorporating this as a built-in tool is probably out of the scope of this PR, but it's a good demonstration of the type of tool mentioned in the proposal that could be written based on this node:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b1383912-80b5-4c95-8ab2-c303c5d42bb8\r\n\r\nAs an alternative (one that I've used before for other tooled mesh gen 🙂) I wrote a quick tool script that, upon save, looks for Marker3D children and makes a hull around them: https://gist.github.com/31/a2fb330e1915ab5be5247a0f2ce43669. Easy to manipulate with the 3d gizmo and quickly duplicate and delete with hotkeys, but messy in the scene tree.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0c48110b-0e91-448d-b5a3-e134066bfd78\r\n\r\nAnd some simple procedural space rock generation at runtime for fun--a random convex orb subtracted from another convex orb. (I had this lying around from earlier attempts at convex hull work, and it works nicely with this node.)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e922a120-98d4-4e1e-ac9d-2863fb7d5d7f\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2559012062/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":6,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2559866171","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2559866171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2559866171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YlHU7","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T15:04:21Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T15:09:22Z","body":"Can it include a `smooth_faces` option like other CSGs?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2559866171/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2559980687","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2559980687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2559980687,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YljSP","user":{"login":"31","id":331300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/331300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/31","html_url":"https://github.com/31","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T16:22:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T16:22:27Z","body":"> Can it include a `smooth_faces` option like other CSGs?\r\n\r\nYeah, it looks like all it does for the the other CSG nodes is mark all vertices as smooth, and I think that's easy enough by post processing the faces after calling `_unpack_manifold`. I'll try to add that.\r\n\r\nManifold offers some fancy smooths like [`SmoothByNormals`, `SmoothOut`, and `Smooth`](https://manifoldcad.org/docs/html/classmanifold_1_1_manifold.html) that could be interesting to try to expose somehow, but I'm not all that familiar with them, and the implications. In the future there could be additional APIs added for those if they do seem interesting--but for now, I think it does make sense to have a basic `smooth` that behaves the same as it does for other CSG nodes.\r\n\r\n(Historical note: I got caught up on this (way) earlier while looking at trying to implement `smooth` and didn't think about simply post processing the faces until after your comment, so thanks for the brain jump start. 😄)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2559980687/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2560061920","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2560061920","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2560061920,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yl3Hg","user":{"login":"31","id":331300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/331300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/31","html_url":"https://github.com/31","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T17:23:01Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T17:23:01Z","body":"Done, I also fixed the inherited `flip_faces` support. For a demo, made a [random-point-sphere tool script](https://gist.github.com/31/de49902ea285bc9b35d2901750f3caae):\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/13423ce0-d5c5-4c0c-b663-77216bb5c27d\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2560061920/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":5,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2562968877","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2562968877","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2562968877,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yw80t","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T17:22:54Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T17:22:54Z","body":"@celyk, I think a proposal for VertexHandles would be good. Thoughts?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2562968877/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2562998485","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2562998485","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2562998485,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxEDV","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T18:08:10Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T18:09:59Z","body":"I think having this in core only really makes sense if there's a built-in way to move its points. Otherwise, you can't use it for grayboxing out of the box, which kind of defeats the point of using CSG to me. (If you're all the way through installing a plugin, you might install [Cyclops Level Builder](https://github.com/blackears/cyclopsLevelBuilder) instead.)\r\n\r\nThere could also be menu options to convert CSGBox3D, CSGSphere3D and CSGCylinder3D to CSGConvexHull3D so you can edit their points, but this can be added later.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2562998485/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563078477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2563078477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2563078477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxXlN","user":{"login":"31","id":331300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/331300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/31","html_url":"https://github.com/31","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T20:25:17Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T21:03:32Z","body":"> I think having this in core only really makes sense if there's a built-in way to move its points. Otherwise, you can't use it for grayboxing out of the box, which kind of defeats the point of using CSG to me.\r\n\r\nThere are other uses for CSG than editor-time level design.\r\n\r\nIn https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9933 I wrote the reason it matters to me: my project involves making a simplified 3d modeling tool for the user. The fact that all this CSG tech is able to run at runtime (unlike similar tech from other game engines) is amazing, and saves me from reimplementing it. However, editor-specific features (the 3d gizmo, a hypothetical point editor) can't be reused at runtime, so they don't help that project.\r\n\r\n(What the player is modeling is essentially level design, so there's crossover. 😄)\r\n\r\nI pointed out another use case at https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2559012062: procedurally generating meshes where the artistic intent is in the algorithm, not any particular point. A point editor makes no difference there either. (That demo is at runtime, but this can be done in the editor too.)\r\n\r\nI don't oppose having a point editor, but I see plenty of reasons to have this node before one is designed/implemented, and I also think a proposal is appropriate.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563078477/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563094733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2563094733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2563094733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxbjN","user":{"login":"31","id":331300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/331300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/31","html_url":"https://github.com/31","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T20:55:41Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T20:55:41Z","body":"> having this in core\r\n\r\nHmm, realized this seems to have a specific meaning, but I might be misinterpreting it. This node is actually in the csg module, not core, right? Does that make a difference?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563094733/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563209025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2563209025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2563209025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yx3dB","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T01:09:24Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T01:09:24Z","body":"> Hmm, realized this seems to have a specific meaning, but I might be misinterpreting it. This node is actually in the csg module, not core, right? Does that make a difference?\r\n\r\nBy \"having this in core\", I meant having this as a core feature of the engine, as opposed to an add-on.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563209025/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563213362","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2563213362","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2563213362,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yx4gy","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T01:19:53Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T01:19:53Z","body":"@31 I think if you port VertexHandles.gd to C++, it would work out of the box. Thoughts? @Calinou ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563213362/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563337525","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2563337525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2563337525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YyW01","user":{"login":"31","id":331300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/331300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/31","html_url":"https://github.com/31","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/31/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T05:34:31Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T05:37:06Z","body":"> I think if you port VertexHandles.gd to C++, it would work out of the box. Thoughts?\r\n\r\nWell, it needs a few features first IMO: a way to create a new point, and a way to delete a point. Not a big problem necessarily--CSGPolygon3D does have a precedent and maybe the implementation could be borrowed: ctrl-click and drag from an existing point (or existing edge?), right click. (I don't see how that's done after looking through `csg_gizmos.cpp`, though.)\r\n\r\nHowever, more generally, I'm not confident that moving points in the camera's perspective plane is sufficient. A CSG user *might* realize that they can use multiple views to edit points along orthographic planes. If you don't realize that or simply prefer to edit using a single perspective camera, it's pretty awkward IMO. I almost didn't realize it before I recorded that video. 😄\r\n\r\nIf it seemed easy, I'd offer to go ahead with it, but I'm not sure I'd be able to make something acceptable.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563337525/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563407147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100725#issuecomment-2563407147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100725","id":2563407147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yyn0r","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}